      "statement": "B&W pitches its gas-fired boiler plus steam turbine (Rankine) plant as a way around gas turbine scarcity — 'no dependence on gas turbine delivery', generating firm MW while gas turbines are still being manufactured, and 'years-faster deployment' than combined- or simple-cycle gas turbine projects. This is the seller's own marketing; no third party has confirmed the time advantage, and B&W's phase 2 adds a gas turbine later (boiler becomes an HRSG), so the route is a bridge as much as a substitute.",
